Not Applicable

Employment type

Full-time

Job function

Engineering and Information Technology

Industries

IT Services and IT Consulting

Accenture Digital Core

At Accenture Digital Core, we help clients innovate continuously, at speed and scale, combining deep industry expertise with cutting-edge technology to deliver real transformation. You'll join projects where innovation, intelligence and technical experience come together to build robust, secure and scalable digital solutions.

What You'll Do

Design, develop and maintain full stack web applications using React on the frontend, .NET Core / .NET Framework on the backend, and SQL Server as the data layer;

Build and consume RESTful APIs across enterprise platforms;

Integrate CI/CD pipelines and participate in production releases using Azure DevOps and Git;

Troubleshoot and resolve production incidents (P1/P2) with a structured approach to incident and problem management;

Ensure code quality, performance and security standards, including authentication flows;

Collaborate with cross-functional and international teams in an Agile delivery context.

What You'll Need

University degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology or a comparable technical field;

5–8 years of experience as a Full Stack Developer in production environments;

Strong knowledge of .NET (C#) and related frameworks;

Frontend development experience with React;

Solid command of SQL and ORM tools (Entity Framework);

Professional English (C1, spoken and written); French or Dutch is a plus;

Ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders;

Proactive mindset with a strong sense of ownership and accountability;

Ability to prioritize and manage workload efficiently in a dynamic environment.

What We Offer

Health insurance;

Life Insurance and Pension Plan Programs;

Free medical services at the office (Physician, Nutritionist, Psychologist);

Wellness programs;

Flexben Program (Support for Education, Kindergarden, Training, Technology, Health);

Employee Share Purchase Plan;

Personalized training paths and access to Udemy and Plurisight Plataforms;

Flex-ability program (financial and flexible support for people with disabilities);

Special banking conditions;

Hybrid working model.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Mid-Senior level

Employment type

Full-time

Job function

Information Technology and Engineering

Industries

Software Development

Challenge yourself and us

At AdvanceWorks, we learn together, grow together, and have fun together. And we do all this while creating great software solutions for clients across many industries and geographies.
We are constantly challenging ourselves and each other to use the latest technologies and the best methodologies, making sure we always walk the talk.

What will be your role

We are looking for a AI Architect
to join the cross-functional architecture team at the heart of a large-scale AI acceleration program. This program is redefining the IT operating model, evolving it into an orchestrated ecosystem of AI agents and specialist skills that spans the full software development lifecycle (SDLC), Data, and Operations. The program runs across multiple execution streams, including development on several platforms, AI testing, observability, data products, and talk2data, with a strong focus on measurable results and impact. As part of the transversal architecture team, you'll ensure coherence, governance, and architectural evolution across every initiative, working closely with the privacy & compliance function and the teams tracking adoption metrics.

Your responsibilities will include

Defining standards and blueprints for integrating AI across the SDLC, Data, and Operations;
Ensuring interoperability between platforms while managing technical debt and legacy migration;
Sizing infrastructure for AI/ML workloads and defining the deployment strategy;
Participating in the Architecture Review Board to validate new initiatives;
Contributing actively to the cross-functional architecture community;

What should you bring to the team

A solid foundation as a software developer, built through years of shipping real production code in Java, .NET, Python, or similar;
Proven experience with AI-native architectures: agent orchestration, LLMs in production, RAG patterns, guardrails, and MCP;
Solid cloud architecture background with a focus on AI/ML workloads, including cost management, rate limiting, and inference caching;
Comfortable across heterogeneous stacks, including OutSystems, Salesforce (Agentforce), open source, event-driven architecture, and microservices, with a modular mindset that avoids vendor lock-in;
Experience in regulated environments (telco, banking, or insurance), with solid knowledge of GDPR and, ideally, the EU AI Act;
Security-by-design mindset applied to AI, paired with CI/CD pipelines featuring AI-powered quality gates and end-to-end observability;
Availability to work in a hybrid model, based in Lisbon;
Fluent Portuguese;

Nice to have

Deeper familiarity with the EU AI Act and its implications for enterprise architecture;
Experience defining AI governance frameworks or centers of excellence;
Background contributing to or leading architecture communities of practice;

What is in it for you

An amazing informal culture of smart, hardworking, and friendly people who support and care about each other;
A mentorship program from day one;
The opportunity to help shape the architecture of a large-scale AI acceleration program, right at the intersection of SDLC, Data, and Operations;
Formal training and certifications;
Access to cutting-edge AI tools and technologies;
A dynamic company where your ideas matter more than your job title;
Flexibility with responsibility;
A Rubber Duck to help you talk through those tricky architecture puzzles;

Don't hold off any longer and apply now! If you have any questions, drop us a line at people@advanceworks.ai
.

